        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"State of AI in 2026: LLMs, Coding, Scaling Laws, China, Agents, GPUs, AGI\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Lex Fridman Podcast #490 with Nathan Lambert & Sebastian Raschka covering LLMs and AI coding capabilities, scaling laws, AI agents, GPU infrastructure, AGI development, and China vs US AI competition.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Lex Fridman Podcast\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-02-01\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\n    10→      \"LLMs\",\n    11→      \"AI coding\",\n    12→      \"scaling laws\",\n    13→      \"AI agents\",\n    14→      \"AGI\"\n    15→    ],\n    16→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    17→  },\n    18→  {\n    19→    \"title\": \"AI coding tools are shifting to a surprising place: The terminal\",\n    20→    \"description\": \"TechCrunch article discussing how AI coding tools are shifting from IDE-based editors to terminal-based workflows, marking a significant evolution in developer tooling.\",\n    21→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    22→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    23→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/15/ai-coding-tools-are-shifting-to-a-surprising-place-the-terminal/\",\n    24→    \"published_date\": \"2025-07-15\",\n    25→    \"topics\": [\n    26→      \"AI coding tools\",\n    27→      \"terminal\",\n    28→      \"developer workflows\",\n    29→      \"CLI tools\"\n    30→    ],\n    31→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    32→  },\n    33→  {\n    34→    \"title\": \"Claws - a new layer on top of LLM agents\",\n    35→    \"description\": \"Posted about 'Claws' as 'a new layer on top of LLM agents,' giving an example of how '/add-telegram instructs your AI agent how to modify the actual code to integrate Telegram'.\",\n    36→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n    37→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    38→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2024987174077432126\",\n    39→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-23\",\n    40→    \"topics\": [\n    41→      \"AI agents\",\n    42→      \"developer tools\",\n    43→      \"LLM orchestration\"\n    44→    ],\n    45→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    46→  },\n    47→  {\n    48→    \"title\": \"LLMs are especially good at code translation\",\n    49→    \"description\": \"Karpathy discussed how 'LLMs are *especially* good at translation compared to de-novo generation because the original code base acts as a kind of [reference/context]'.\",\n    50→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n    51→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    52→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2023476423055601903\",\n    53→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-22\",\n    54→    \"topics\": [\n    55→      \"LLM capabilities\",\n    56→      \"code translation\",\n    57→      \"AI coding patterns\"\n    58→    ],\n    59→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    60→  },\n    61→  {\n    62→    \"title\": \"Imagination is the only limit - AI coding agents demo\",\n    63→    \"description\": \"Amjad challenges the notion that AI coding agents can only build basic, cookie-cutter apps, stating he proved this wrong with a major public demo showing advanced capabilities.\",\n    64→    \"author\": \"Amjad Masad\",\n    65→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    66→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/amasad/status/2029236003991613828\",\n    67→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-22\",\n    68→    \"topics\": [\n    69→      \"AI coding agents\",\n    70→      \"Replit\",\n    71→      \"demonstration\"\n    72→    ],\n    73→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    74→  },\n    75→  {\n    76→    \"title\": \"In the AI age, coding capabilities belong to everyone\",\n    77→    \"description\": \"He emphasizes that in the AI age, coding capabilities belong to everyone, especially entrepreneurs. Mentions the rise of agentic coding tools like Replit has caused changes in development costs.\",\n    78→    \"author\": \"Amjad Masad\",\n    79→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    80→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/amasad/status/2030370182791840175\",\n    81→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-21\",\n    82→    \"topics\": [\n    83→      \"AI accessibility\",\n    84→      \"entrepreneurship\",\n    85→      \"Replit\"\n    86→    ],\n    87→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    88→  },\n    89→  {\n    90→    \"title\": \"How I write software with LLMs\",\n    91→    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion featuring first-hand developer experience using LLMs for software development with practical insights on integrating LLMs into coding workflows.\",\n    92→    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n    93→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    94→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47394022\",\n    95→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-21\",\n    96→    \"topics\": [\n    97→      \"LLM coding\",\n    98→      \"developer workflow\",\n    99→      \"practical insights\"\n   100→    ],\n   101→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   102→  },\n   103→  {\n   104→    \"title\": \"Shift in LLM coding capability - from 80% manual to more agent usage\",\n   105→    \"description\": \"Karpathy shared notes about 'coding quite a bit' and mentioned the 'latest lift in LLM coding capability,' noting he shifted from '80% manual+autocomplete coding and 20% agents'.\",\n   106→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n   107→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   108→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876\",\n   109→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-20\",\n   110→    \"topics\": [\n   111→      \"AI coding workflow\",\n   112→      \"LLM capabilities\",\n   113→      \"developer productivity\"\n   114→    ],\n   115→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   116→  },\n   117→  {\n   118→    \"title\": \"Vibe coding tools capability shift\",\n   119→    \"description\": \"Amjad discusses 'vibe coding tools' that enable marketers and small business owners to describe applications in plain English and have them running in minutes, describing this as a significant capability shift.\",\n   120→    \"author\": \"Amjad Masad\",\n   121→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   122→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/amasad\",\n   123→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-20\",\n   124→    \"topics\": [\n   125→      \"vibe coding\",\n   126→      \"AI accessibility\",\n   127→      \"low-code development\"\n   128→    ],\n   129→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   130→  },\n   131→  {\n   132→    \"title\": \"Hacker News now thinks coding is solved\",\n   133→    \"description\": \"Reddit discussion debating whether coding is truly being 'solved' by AI and questioning if Hacker News has become overly optimistic about AI capabilities.\",\n   134→    \"author\": \"Reddit Community\",\n   135→    \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   136→    \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/theprimeagen/comments/1qyniqq/hacker_news_now_thinks_coding_is_solved/\",\n   137→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-20\",\n   138→    \"topics\": [\n   139→      \"AI coding\",\n   140→      \"skepticism\",\n   141→      \"future of programming\"\n   142→    ],\n   143→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   144→  },\n   145→  {\n   146→    \"title\": \"I've never felt this much behind as a programmer\",\n   147→    \"description\": \"Notable tweet where Karpathy stated: 'I've never felt this much behind as a programmer. The profession is being dramatically refactored as the bits...'\",\n   148→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n   149→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   150→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2004607146781278521\",\n   151→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-19\",\n   152→    \"topics\": [\n   153→      \"AI impact on programming\",\n   154→      \"developer workflow\",\n   155→      \"future of coding\"\n   156→    ],\n   157→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   158→  },\n   159→  {\n   160→    \"title\": \"Coding agents have replaced every framework I used\",\n   161→    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion about AI coding agents replacing traditional development frameworks and exploring implications of AI-assisted development workflows.\",\n   162→    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n   163→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   164→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46923543\",\n   165→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-19\",\n   166→    \"topics\": [\n   167→      \"AI coding agents\",\n   168→      \"frameworks\",\n   169→      \"development workflows\"\n   170→    ],\n   171→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   172→  },\n   173→  {\n   174→    \"title\": \"Claude Code / AI that lives on your computer\",\n   175→    \"description\": \"Karpathy discussed Claude Code as 'the first convincing demonstration of what an LLM Agent looks like' - highlighting it as a significant milestone in AI agent development.\",\n   176→    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n   177→    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n   178→    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2002118205729562949\",\n   179→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-18\",\n   180→    \"topics\": [\n   181→      \"LLM agents\",\n   182→      \"Claude Code\",\n   183→      \"AI coding\"\n   184→    ],\n   185→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   186→  },\n   187→  {\n   188→    \"title\": \"How to make vibe coding not suck\",\n   189→    \"description\": \"Fireship critique of AI 'vibe coding' practices with best practices for AI-assisted development and modern programming workflows.\",\n   190→    \"author\": \"Fireship\",\n   191→    \"source\": \"YouTube\",\n   192→    \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLKrSVuT-Dg\",\n   193→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-18\",\n   194→    \"topics\": [\n   195→      \"vibe coding\",\n   196→      \"AI-assisted development\",\n   197→      \"best practices\"\n   198→    ],\n   199→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   200→  },\n   201→  {\n   202→    \"title\": \"AI doesn't reduce work, it intensifies it\",\n   203→    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion challenging the narrative that AI reduces developer workload, exploring how AI tools require programming skills to be effective.\",\n   204→    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n   205→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   206→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46955703\",\n   207→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-17\",\n   208→    \"topics\": [\n   209→      \"AI impact\",\n   210→      \"developer workload\",\n   211→      \"programming skills\"\n   212→    ],\n   213→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   214→  },\n   215→  {\n   216→    \"title\": \"OpenAI just made your entire tech stack obsolete\",\n   217→    \"description\": \"Fireship video covering the Junie coding agent for JetBrains IDE and discussing OpenAI DevDay 2025 announcements about AI coding tools.\",\n   218→    \"author\": \"Fireship\",\n   219→    \"source\": \"YouTube\",\n   220→    \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=91aH8jsG4cc\",\n   221→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-15\",\n   222→    \"topics\": [\n   223→      \"AI coding tools\",\n   224→      \"OpenAI\",\n   225→      \"JetBrains\",\n   226→      \"developer tools\"\n   227→    ],\n   228→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   229→  },\n   230→  {\n   231→    \"title\": \"My Bleeding Edge Tech Stack for 2025\",\n   232→    \"description\": \"Fireship AI-driven development masterclass covering modern programming workflows and the bleeding edge tech stack for 2025.\",\n   233→    \"author\": \"Fireship\",\n   234→    \"source\": \"YouTube\",\n   235→    \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rFP7rUYtOOg\",\n   236→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-12\",\n   237→    \"topics\": [\n   238→      \"AI development\",\n   239→      \"tech stack\",\n   240→      \"programming workflows\"\n   241→    ],\n   242→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   243→  },\n   244→  {\n   245→    \"title\": \"Here's how I use LLMs to help me write code\",\n   246→    \"description\": \"Discusses the challenges and unintuitive nature of using LLMs for coding. Explores how to effectively leverage LLMs as complementary tools rather than replacements. Simon emphasizes practical LLM integration in developer workflows.\",\n   247→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   248→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   249→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2025/Mar/11/using-llms-for-code/\",\n   250→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-11\",\n   251→    \"topics\": [\n   252→      \"LLM coding\",\n   253→      \"developer workflow\",\n   254→      \"AI-assisted development\"\n   255→    ],\n   256→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   257→  },\n   258→  {\n   259→    \"title\": \"Enhancing LLM Code Generation through Test-Driven Development\",\n   260→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper on improving LLM code generation capabilities using TDD methodologies, reflecting growing emphasis on practical improvement techniques for code LLMs.\",\n   261→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n   262→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   263→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12823\",\n   264→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-10\",\n   265→    \"topics\": [\n   266→      \"code generation\",\n   267→      \"TDD\",\n   268→      \"LLM improvement\",\n   269→      \"practical techniques\"\n   270→    ],\n   271→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   272→  },\n   273→  {\n   274→    \"title\": \"Increasing LLM Coding Capabilities through Diverse Synthetic Data\",\n   275→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper tackling the limitation of progress in code generation due to data shortages by using diverse synthetic data to boost model performance.\",\n   276→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n   277→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   278→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.23208\",\n   279→    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-09\",\n   280→    \"topics\": [\n   281→      \"code generation\",\n   282→      \"synthetic data\",\n   283→      \"LLM training\",\n   284→      \"data augmentation\"\n   285→    ],\n   286→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   287→  },\n   288→  {\