d at code translation\",\n    \"description\": \"Karpathy discussed how 'LLMs are *especially* good at translation compared to de-novo generation because the original code base acts as a kind of [reference/context]'.\",\n    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    \"url\": \"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2023476423055601903\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"LLM capabilities\",\n      \"code translation\",\n      \"AI coding patterns\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Imagination is the only limit - AI coding agents demo\",\n    \"description\": \"Amjad challenges the notion that AI coding agents can only build basic, cookie-cutter apps, stating he proved this wrong with a major public demo showing advanced capabilities.\",\n    \"author\": \"Amjad Masad\",\n    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    \"url\": \"https://x.com/amasad/status/2029236003991613828\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI coding agents\",\n      \"Replit\",\n      \"demonstration\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"In the AI age, coding capabilities belong to everyone\",\n    \"description\": \"He emphasizes that in the AI age, coding capabilities belong to everyone, especially entrepreneurs. Mentions the rise of agentic coding tools like Replit has caused changes in development costs.\",\n    \"author\": \"Amjad Masad\",\n    \"source\": \"Twitter\",\n    \"url\": \"https://x.com/amasad/status/2030370182791840175\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2025-03-21\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI accessibility\",\n      \"entrepreneurship\",\n      \"Replit\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"How I write software with LLMs\",\n    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion featuring first-hand developer experience using LLMs for software development with practical insights on integrating LLMs into coding workflows.\",\n